Fix an axis-parallel rectangle $R \subset \mathbb{Z}^d$. For $x \in \mathbb{Z}^d$ and $r > 0$, let $R(x,r)$ denote the translate of $R$ by $x$ and scaled by a factor of $r$. The proof is identical to that for boxes.

We define
\begin{equation}
    \delta_{R}(A,B)
    =
    \liminf_{\substack{x \in \mathbb{Z}^d,\; r \to \infty \\
    \frac{|R(x,r)\cap B|}{\log^2 r} \to \infty}}
    \frac{|R(x,r)\cap B \cap A|}{|R(x,r)\cap B|}.
    \label{eq:banachdimd2}
\end{equation}
